Created On
11/03/2025
Created By
Kristie Lines
Activity Comments
Released By: EN411KL
riveway specifications:

If doing paved driveway all components of the paved portion of the driveway must be set back from the edge of the unpaved travel way. The driveway apron must maintain a 3'' minimum set back from the travel way. If doing unpaved apron ignore the asphalt or concrete and build it from limerock, dirt and/or stone.

Install a 15" diameter culvert pipe, a minimum of a 5’ covered space must exist between edge of the driveway apron and the top of the mitered end section on both sides of the paved apron. Need a paved apron minimum of 10'' wide at right-of-way/property line. Due to road classification, 5'' radius are required on each side of the driveway. The driveway must extend a minimum of one-foot past the property line.

All driveway aprons shall be a minimum of 6" of reinforced concrete over 6" of stabilized cover or 1 1/4" of SP 9.5 asphalt over 6" of compacted and primed limerock. Concrete shall be 3000 psi, reinforced with 6x6x10 welded wire, and raised a minimum of 1" off ground. Concrete drives with culverts may use the saddle method. Contact the Marion county right-of-way division for details.

Concrete mitered end sections are not required to be installed as part of this permit, however, if the applicant chooses to do so, the concrete mitered ends must be formed up to current LDC specifications

Right-of- way restoration:

LDC 7.1.3. Construction specifications reference 0. Grassing and ts022.

Stabilize with one row of sod around the apron, at the edge of the road and in the ditch bottom of the disturbed right- of- way, the rest of the ROW can be seed and mulch. Sod shall be established, well-rooted common Bermuda grass, St. Augustine grass, Centipede grass, Pensacola Bahia grass or Argentine Bahia grass except that where sod replaces or is adjacent to established private lawns, similar grass material to that existing shall be used. Sod shall be alive, fresh and uninjured at the time of planting. Mulch material shall be dry straw of hay or oats, rye, Bermuda or Bahia grass free of weeds and undesirable grasses. This needs to be completed prior to a final inspection.

Modifications to the driveway specifications requires prior approval from the office of the county engineer.

ROW 11/3/25 Mike'
